* mq-observability-pack - queue manager objects for the lab. Keep this file ASCII-only.
* Runs automatically at start (any /etc/mqm/*.mqsc). Idempotent: REPLACE everywhere.
* The MQ Advanced for Developers image already defines DEV.QUEUE.1..3, DEV.DEAD.LETTER.QUEUE,
* DEV.APP.SVRCONN (user app) and DEV.ADMIN.SVRCONN (user admin).

* --- Turn on every monitoring source the pack relies on --------------------
* MONQ/MONCHL(HIGH): queue/channel real-time monitoring -> QTIME, MSGAGE, LGETDATE etc. (DIS QSTATUS)
* STATQ/STATMQI/STATCHL: statistics event messages (SYSTEM.ADMIN.STATISTICS.QUEUE), also feeds $SYS topics
* PERFMEV: queue-depth performance events (QDPHIEV/QDEPTHHI) -> SYSTEM.ADMIN.PERFM.EVENT
* STATINT(60): statistics interval seconds (default 1800 is useless for a lab)
ALTER QMGR MONQ(HIGH) MONCHL(HIGH) STATQ(ON) STATMQI(ON) STATCHL(HIGH) STATINT(60) PERFMEV(ENABLED) CHLEV(ENABLED) LOCALEV(ENABLED) REMOTEEV(ENABLED) STRSTPEV(ENABLED)

* --- Application queues ---------------------------------------------------
DEFINE QLOCAL('APP.ORDERS.REQ') REPLACE DESCR('Orders request queue (producer->consumer)') MAXDEPTH(5000) MONQ(HIGH) STATQ(ON) QDPHIEV(ENABLED) QDEPTHHI(80) QDPLOEV(ENABLED) QDEPTHLO(20) DEFPSIST(YES)
DEFINE QLOCAL('APP.ORDERS.RSP') REPLACE DESCR('Orders response queue') MAXDEPTH(5000) MONQ(HIGH) STATQ(ON) DEFPSIST(YES)
DEFINE QLOCAL('APP.BURST')      REPLACE DESCR('Chaos target: small MAXDEPTH, flooded by queue-full experiment') MAXDEPTH(200) MONQ(HIGH) STATQ(ON) QDPHIEV(ENABLED) QDEPTHHI(80) DEFPSIST(NO)
DEFINE QLOCAL('APP.CANARY')     REPLACE DESCR('Synthetic put/get canary') MAXDEPTH(1000) MONQ(HIGH) STATQ(ON) DEFPSIST(NO)
DEFINE QLOCAL('APP.DLQ')        REPLACE DESCR('Application dead-letter queue') MAXDEPTH(100000) MONQ(HIGH) STATQ(ON)
ALTER QMGR DEADQ('APP.DLQ')

* --- Authority: the `app` user (DEV.APP.SVRCONN) may put/get/inq/browse on APP.* ----
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('APP.**') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(BROWSE,GET,INQ,PUT,DSP)
SET AUTHREC OBJTYPE(QMGR) PRINCIPAL('app') AUTHADD(CONNECT,INQ,DSP)

* --- Exporter needs DIS QSTATUS/CHSTATUS + $SYS subscriptions: admin already has it via mqm group.
* Larger MAXHANDS: mq_prometheus opens one subscription per monitored queue x class.
ALTER QMGR MAXHANDS(2048)

* --- $SYS/MQ monitoring publications must never reach the dead-letter queue. SYSTEM.ADMIN.TOPIC
* ships with USEDLQ(YES) and the whole $SYS subtree inherits it (DIS TPSTATUS shows it), so an
* exporter that stops being scraped fills its temporary reply queue (MAXDEPTH 5000, ~20 min)
* and every further publication is dead-lettered at ~4/s: a false IBMMQDeadLetterQueueNotEmpty
* on a healthy queue manager (seen live on 2026-09-16). NPMSGDLV(ALLAVAIL) then discards the
* undeliverable non-persistent copy instead.
ALTER TOPIC('SYSTEM.ADMIN.TOPIC') USEDLQ(NO)

* --- Listener: the image creates the qmgr with `crtmqm -p 1414`, i.e. SYSTEM.LISTENER.TCP.1
* CONTROL(QMGR). Chaos scenario `listener-stopped` uses STOP/START LISTENER on that name plus
* STOP CHANNEL(...) MODE(FORCE) on both DEV.*.SVRCONN channels: stopping the listener alone
* leaves established client conversations working.
